# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Godot 4 — Fiel al Libro
#  Rules of the repo (see TECH_STACK.md §3.5)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Private design documents.
#
#  GDD.md holds the full design: the thesis, the endings, the DLC plan, the
#  IP and cultural-sensitivity rules.
#  docs/IP_CLEARANCE.md holds the title clearance memo: it names
#  competitors, their positioning and their weaknesses.
#
#  Both stay on this machine only, and are deliberately kept OUT of git
#  history (not just untracked) so they cannot be recovered from a previous
#  commit.
#
#  The public repo carries the implementation and the supporting docs
#  (README, TECH_STACK, ROADMAP, TODO).
#
#  To publish either later: remove the line and `git add <path>`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GDD.md
docs/IP_CLEARANCE.md

# Godot's import cache and per-machine settings. NEVER commit: it contains
# absolute paths and will conflict on every machine.
.godot/
/android/

# Screenshots and playtest captures. Local only: they are outputs,
# not sources, and the repo should not fill up with them. The .gdignore
# IS committed, so Godot never imports them into a build.
/artifacts/*
!/artifacts/.gdignore

# Exported builds
/build/
/export/
*.exe
*.pck
*.zip

# Export presets: desktop platforms carry no secrets, so export_presets.cfg
# IS committed (CI needs it to build). If you add an Android/iOS target,
# move its keystore and credentials into a template instead.
export_credentials.cfg

# Godot's own cache / logs
*.translation.import
logs/
*.log

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  LFS-tracked binary formats are declared in .gitattributes
#  Blender scenes, textures, audio and fonts are LFS; the .import sidecar
#  files stay as plain text so import presets survive a fresh clone.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
